    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2611.18064v1</id>
    <title>A$^3$: Adaptive Audio Agent Framework for Collaborative Edge Computing</title>
    <updated>2026-11-13T11:48:16Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.18064v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2611.18064v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>Embedded audio agents need a nearby edge server for speed, but a server-dependent agent returns nothing when the link fails. We present A$^3$, an adaptive audio agent framework that places whole pipeline stages on the server, keeps a complete fallback agent on devices that can host one, and hedges both paths with a link-aware deadline that decides when to give up on the server. On Jetson devices and an RTX A4500 server, A$^3$ matches the server-only agent on a healthy link, answers every request in a full outage on the AGX, and beats a percentile hedge in simulated outages.</summary>
    <category term="cs.AI" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
