    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2611.18035v1</id>
    <title>RL$^{\mathrm{RT}}$: On-Device Reinforcement Learning Runtime</title>
    <updated>2026-11-13T11:05:04Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.18035v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2611.18035v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>On-device reinforcement learning runs a periodic actor and a learner on one embedded GPU shared with other workloads. Because the learner produces the actor's weights, existing designs stall the actor or let its policy drift. We present RL$^{\mathrm{RT}}$, an on-device runtime that makes this coupling a tunable parameter: a refresh bound limits actor releases between refreshes, and a GPU permit with slack-aware admission prioritises the actor and fills spare time with training atop any base scheduler. Under the real refresh cost on two Jetson boards, RL$^{\mathrm{RT}}$ keeps a 16.8 M-parameter policy's deadline misses below 1%, against 85 to 100% without it.</summary>
    <category term="cs.LG" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
