    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2611.17938v1</id>
    <title>Measured from the feed: the unsustainable growth of AI video generation</title>
    <updated>2026-11-13T09:21:46Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.17938v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2611.17938v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>Text-to-video generation runs at commercial scale, but its broader environmental impacts remain, to our knowledge, understudied. Providers rarely disclose video volumes or energy needs; we measured the yearly video output of two commercial platforms and built a prospective model of such services' absolute footprint from training to storage. Our projections suggest that reducing emissions depends on both limiting growth in video generation and achieving substantial efficiency gains. Under continued growth, emissions rise nearly seventy-five-fold by 2030 despite technological improvements. When usage remains at 2026 levels, the same improvements reduce emissions by about two-fifths. These estimates are a conservative lower bound: they cover one AI service among many; other services and uses would push the total higher.</summary>
    <category term="cs.AI" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
