    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2611.17881v1</id>
    <title>Photogrammetric 3D Model-Based Animal Behavior Classification</title>
    <updated>2026-11-13T08:15:39Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.17881v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2611.17881v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>Video-based behavior estimation is often implemented end-to-end from image sequences. We advocate a two-stage alternative: reconstruct 3D body and object geometry before classifying behavior. This makes ambiguities of the ill-posed 2D-to-3D inverse problem explicit and potentially correctable. We demonstrate the strategy with simulated interacting mice and extend it to real video.</summary>
